-- Interval transport through log (image: the whole line, so no clamp; its
-- inverse exp is total). log x > 0 iff x > 1: 1 - Phi(1). The False arm
-- keeps the -inf endpoint untouched (x < 1, Phi(1)) rather than exp(-inf) = 0:
-- for x <= 0 the forward log is NaN and NaN > 0 is False on every backend, so
-- that is also what sampling answers.
main = let x = Normal in if log x > 0.0 then 1.0 else 0.0
